Q: What's the difference between Amazon SNS and Amazon SQS in terms of message delivery?
A:
SNS:
* Push-based messaging (actively pushes to subscribers)
* One message, multiple receivers (pub/sub model)
* Can send to multiple types of endpoints:
    * SQS queues
    * Lambda functions
    * HTTP/S endpoints
    * Mobile push notifications
    * Email
* Messages are not persisted (lost if not delivered)
SQS:
* Pull-based messaging (consumers poll for messages)
* One message, one receiver (queue model)
* Messages persist until processed
* Messages can be processed later
* Consumers must actively retrieve messages

